    "criterion": "IMPLEMENTED 2026-08-23. WHEN PricingTable::seed() is built, THE SYSTEM SHALL source the bulk of its PricingRate rows from a vendored copy of LiteLLM's community-maintained model_prices_and_context_window.json (github.com/BerriAI/litellm, crates/lumen-model/data/litellm_model_prices.json), refreshed via the explicit `just update-pricing` task, NOT from hand-typed Rust literals -- the staleness of hand-typed literals was the direct cause of CRIT-LUMEN-008's real overcharge/undercharge bug (2026-08-21, every current real model on a real machine mispriced). rate_for/normalize_model_key/is_recognized's lookup logic is unaffected -- only seed()'s data source changed, in crates/lumen-model/src/pricing_source.rs's load_vendored_rates. Only \"mode\": \"chat\" entries under a direct first-party litellm_provider (anthropic, openai, gemini, vertex_ai-language-models -- the providers Lumen's four known adapters actually draw from; gateway/regional resale listings like bedrock_converse or azure_ai are excluded) are loaded; a pricing field LiteLLM omits produces no row, never an invented value (this corrected two prior hand-typed approximations: gpt-4o and gemini-2.0-flash were assumed to have no separate cache-write charge and priced writes at the input rate, but LiteLLM publishes no cache-write field for either at all, so CacheWrite now correctly returns 0.0 per CRIT-LUMEN-161; gpt-5.6-terra's cache-write rate was assumed equal to its input rate but is actually a real, distinct, higher published rate). A small hand-typed layer remains in PricingTable::seed() for real, previously-verified models that have since rolled off LiteLLM's current snapshot entirely (claude-3-5-sonnet, claude-3-5-haiku, qwen-2.5-coder, claude-opus [v3], deepseek-r1, kimi-k1.5, glm-4-plus, gemini-2.0-pro) -- since Lumen prices historical sessions, a model disappearing from LiteLLM's *current* file must not make real past sessions using it go unpriced. LiteLLM's cache_creation_input_token_cost_above_1hr field was confirmed to match Lumen's 1h-cache-tier need exactly (verified against real Opus 5/Sonnet 5/Haiku 4.5/Fable 5 rates: every field byte-for-byte identical to the prior hand-typed values). Never fetched live: `just update-pricing` is an explicit, reviewed re-vendor step, not a per-request fetch, preserving point-in-time-stable historical pricing.",
