    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-171",
    "criterion": "IMPLEMENTED 2026-08-23. WHEN a cost value is surfaced to a caller that will display or report it, THE SYSTEM SHALL make it structurally difficult to read a dollar figure without also observing whether it is genuinely priced -- via lumen_model::Cost, a sum type (Priced(f64) | Unpriced) obtained from TokenEconomics::cost()/ModelTokenSummary::cost()/lumen_store::SessionSummaryReadModel::cost(), whose Unpriced case must be matched to obtain a number at all. total_cost_usd/is_fully_priced themselves remain the underlying (f64, bool) representation -- required for turn/session cost summation and SQL persistence, both of which need the raw numeric value regardless of pricing status -- Cost is specifically the accessor for the point a cost is surfaced to a human (a CLI table, a report), not a replacement for the stored fields.",
