    "judgment_call": true,
    "reasoning": "Audit + research finding (2026-08-22): the float-plus-bool representation is exactly what let ClaudeCodeAdapter's stale model_family default (claude.rs:37, a separate confirmed HIGH bug from the same audit) produce a real, silently-wrong cost for an unknown period without any test catching it -- the type system permitted reading total_cost_usd while ignoring is_fully_priced. Research confirmed no external prior art solves this for us (OpenTelemetry's GenAI semantic conventions explicitly leave cost/pricing representation to the consumer entirely) -- this is a Lumen-specific type-modeling decision. Implemented 2026-08-23 as a Cost enum surfaced via .cost() methods rather than replacing the stored (f64, bool) pair everywhere: lumen-store's SQL persistence and lumen-analysis's cross-turn cost summation both genuinely need the raw numeric representation, so the fix targets the actual display/report boundary the criterion's own wording already scoped it to ('at the point cost is surfaced to callers'). Surveying every real total_cost_usd/is_fully_priced call site to apply this (lumen-cli's 3 display sites) surfaced a second, more severe real bug, now tracked separately as SPEC-LUMEN-003-STORE.json's CRIT-LUMEN-175: is_fully_priced had no backing column in lumen-store's sessions/token_usage tables at all, so it was silently lost on every store round-trip (hardcoded true on read-back) -- lumen-cli's `sessions` command read total_cost_usd with literally no is_fully_priced check, the exact bug class this criterion exists to make impossible, live in the store layer. Fixed in the same pass."
