    "reasoning": "Audit finding (2026-08-22, adversarially verified): unlike lumen-analysis's RawMessageAccumulators, which carry a documented rationale for their exclusion from AnalyticsEngine, nothing explained why these six repositories existed unconsumed. Investigating concretely (2026-08-23) found ToolCallRepository was a materially different case from the other five: its READ side (tool_counts_by_session/error_counts_by_session) was already wired into SessionRepository::get_session and already shipped in SessionDetailReadModel's serialized/CLI output -- so tool_counts/error_counts were an already-advertised feature that silently always returned empty for every real session, not merely an unbuilt one. Wiring its write side was a real but bounded fix (the data already exists on CanonicalTranscript; the only new judgment calls were an intent_kind string mapping, defaulting an unmatched call's is_error to false, and approximating per-call latency_ms from the owning turn's total, all documented inline). The other five have no such existing read-side promise and each needs real, distinct new feature work with no existing caller to build from: FindingsRepository needs a rule/detection engine that doesn't exist yet (nothing computes a Finding from a real session today); QueueRepository and SnapshotRepository are for async/incremental ingestion and already explicitly reserved for a future lumen-daemon consumer (SPEC-LUMEN-004-DAEMON.json); RollupRepository needs a period-aggregation job that doesn't exist yet (nothing calls upsert_rollup in production either); CommandEventRepository needs real shell-command extraction from ToolIntent (its variants -- VersionControl{action}, TestExecution{runner}, Other{raw_name} -- don't cleanly decompose into CommandEventFactRecord's command_base + sanitized_args shape the way tool-call data cleanly decomposed into ToolCallFactRecord). Building any of these five now would be speculative feature work with no demonstrated need, the exact pattern this project already reversed once this session (see the ReadContractEnvelope/versioned-migration-chain build-then-revert, commits 0433201/b6a5f67/4176a77) -- deferred, not resolved by building, consistent with that standing lesson."
